.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ferry-identity 1  Ferry "Ferry Manual"
.SH NAME
ferry\-identity \- Show, back up or restore this device\*(Aqs identity (its Node ID key)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBferry identity\fR [\fB\-\-lang\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show, back up or restore this device\*(Aqs identity (its Node ID key)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fI<CODE>\fR
Interface language for this run (`en`, `pl`); overrides the saved setting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ferry\-identity\-show(1)
Show the Node ID and where the key is stored
.TP
ferry\-identity\-export(1)
Write a backup of the key to a new file (keep it secret)
.TP
ferry\-identity\-storage(1)
Show or change where the key is kept: `file` (default) or `system` (Secret Service / KWallet / GNOME Keyring on Linux, Credential Manager on Windows)
.TP
ferry\-identity\-import(1)
Replace this device\*(Aqs key with one from a backup
